title: PowerShell In-Memory Assembly Load
id: 82dab48a-3172-4d65-b3fc-77913d8c4626
status: experimental
description: Detects reflective loading of a .NET assembly in PowerShell ([Reflection.Assembly]::Load with a byte array), a fileless technique to run tooling entirely in memory and bypass on-disk detection.
author: Alaris Global
references:
  - https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1620/
logsource:
  product: windows
  category: process_creation
detection:
  selection:
    CommandLine|contains:
      - '[Reflection.Assembly]::Load'
      - 'System.Reflection.Assembly]::Load'
      - '.Load([byte[]]'
      - 'FromBase64String'
  condition: selection
fields:
  - CommandLine
  - Image
  - ParentImage
falsepositives:
  - Legitimate in-memory .NET usage
level: high
tags:
  - attack.defense_evasion
  - attack.t1620
